-- these rows to satisfy its foreign keys. At that revision the table has fewer
-- columns than it does at head, so only the columns that exist then are written.
-- The numbered file for the same table re-inserts these at head; `on conflict do
-- nothing` makes that a no-op, which is why the two may overlap.
